A||||1||Minong||Wobbly Driveshafts
Z||000000||Minong||06-13-99||07:55 PM||||<br>I've had CV noise from the passenger rear of the car.  While investigating today, I noticed that there is a lot of movement where the axel enters the auto trans.  Not only end play, but considerable wobbliness.  The driver's side seems to have some movement, but not as much.<p>Is this normal?  If not, what needs to be replaced?
Z||000001||theogre||06-14-99||07:21 AM||||the shaft if it's bad. the trans seal, and the sleave bearing.<p>the sleave may be best left to a trans shop. you need a tool to get it out, and another tool to put in the new one. if you don't have the tools, you'll likely do some damage to the trans. You can buy the tools, you might could rent them, or sign them out at pep boys, but you can't do it without them.
